WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:01.160
MEGAN O'KEEFE: Hi.

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.015
I'm Megan O'Keefe.

00:00:02.015 --> 00:00:03.390
AMEER ABBAS: And
I'm Ameer Abbas,

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.662
and we're both part of the
Google Cloud Platform team.

00:00:05.662 --> 00:00:07.620
Our job is to make Cloud
easier, and we do this

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.830
by creating demos, posting them
on GitHub, doing presentations.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.070
As a matter of fact, we're here
at KubeCon 2019 in San Diego.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.768
We had a great presentation
about virtual machines

00:00:16.768 --> 00:00:18.310
as part of your
Kubernetes ecosystem.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.770
Now I know what
you're all thinking,

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.900
what are we talking about
virtual machines at a KubeCon?

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.567
The harsh reality is
that most customers

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:25.560
we talk to all have
virtual machines running

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.435
in their environment.

00:00:26.435 --> 00:00:29.187
These could be databases,
legacy staple applications.

00:00:29.187 --> 00:00:31.020
Even if they're migrating
their applications

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.580
over to Kubernetes,
they need a way

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.870
to talk to these applications.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.330
And for that, we're using
Istio, which is a service mesh

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.830
technology that Megan is
going to talk a little bit

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:38.200
more about.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.533
MEGAN O'KEEFE: Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:41.820
So the way to incorporate
a virtual machine

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.680
into an Istio service
mesh running on Kubernetes

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.700
is really easy.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.090
All you have to do is
install the Istio sidecar

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:52.440
proxy and the Istio node
agent on the virtual machine,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.360
and then configure it
to call home to Istio

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.620
running on the cluster.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.410
Once you do that, it's really
easy to see all of the metrics

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.250
and logs for both pod and
VM workloads in one place.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.500
And it's really easy
to apply policies

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.650
like role-based access
control and encryption

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.090
on both environments.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.680
If you're interested
in learning more,

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.010
check out
bit.ly/life-outside-the-cluster.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.510
Thanks.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.468
AMEER ABBAS: Thank you.

00:01:15.468 --> 00:01:18.720
[MUSIC PLAYING]

